{"name":"Gold Vessel","hex":"#eaba8a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gold","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy yellow elemental metal of great value, with atomic number 79.","A coin or coinage made of this material, or supposedly so."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["☉ (alchemy)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gold"},{"term":"vessel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A craft for transportation on or in water, air, or space.\n  Any craft designed for transportation on or in water, such as a ship, boat, or submarine. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Any craft designed for transportation on or in water, such as a ship, boat, or submarine. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put into a vessel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vessel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vessel (Twenty One Pilots album)","blocks":[{"text":"Vessel is the third studio album by the American musical duo Twenty One Pilots, which was released on January 8, 2013. It is the band's first album released via Fueled by Ramen, and is their major-label debut album. Vessel debuted at number 58 on the Billboard 200 chart, but reached its peak at number 21 in 2016 following the duo's mainstream breakthrough. As of July 2019, the album has sold over two million equivalent album units in the U.S. All of its tracks have been certified at least Gold by the RIAA, which made Twenty One Pilots the first group or artist to achieve this feat with two separate albums. The album received positive reviews from critics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0f/Twenty_One_Pilots_-_Vessel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vessel_(Twenty_One_Pilots_album)","wikidata":"Q7923335"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","wikidata":"Q897"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Twenty_one_pilots_4.jpg/500px-Twenty_one_pilots_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Twenty_one_pilots_4.jpg/1280px-Twenty_one_pilots_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Twenty_one_pilots_4.jpg/500px-Twenty_one_pilots_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Frontman Tyler Joseph performing during the Quiet Is Violent World Tour in 2014","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwenty_one_pilots_4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d5/Beowulf_-_gold.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d5/Beowulf_-_gold.jpg?utm_source=en.wi